WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:08.645
In the Encyclopedia of Triangle Centers, the Euler Line is the foundational central line discovered by Leonhard Euler in seventeen sixty-five.

2
00:00:08.645 --> 00:00:17.970
In every non-equilateral triangle, the Centroid X two, the Circumcenter X three, the Orthocenter X four, and the Nine-Point Center X five are strictly collinear.

3
00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:30.214
Because the medial triangle and reference triangle A B C are homothetic at the Centroid X two with scale factor negative one-half, the orthocenter of the medial triangle is the circumcenter X three of A B C.

4
00:00:30.214 --> 00:00:36.440
Consequently, X two lies between X three and X four at exactly one-third the distance from X three to X four.

5
00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:51.060
The Nine-Point Center X five bisects segment X three X four, creating the canonical Euler segment ratios: X three to X two, X two to X five, and X five to X four stand in the exact proportion two to one to three.
